    "did_you_know": "A mark showing a square with a dot at the center is on the inside of this helmet; so far it is unidentified.",
    "description": "A bevor is a piece of plate armor that is intended to protect the chin and upper throat. It normally supplemented an open helmet like the sallet. Gothic plate armor achieves its beauty not by surface decoration by the simple elegance of its line, seemingly inspired by contemporary gothic architecture, from which it gets its name.",
